{#
/**
 * @file
 * Row wrapper for the Selected work view.
 *
 * This element is the direct parent of the case-study cards, so the grid
 * lives here rather than on the page or in the view's configuration.
 *
 * One column on small screens, two from md up. Six cards make three even
 * rows; `items-stretch` keeps cards in a row the same height so their lower
 * thirds line up.
 */
#}
{% if title %}
  <h2>{{ title }}</h2>
{% endif %}

{#
  Cards were briefly rotated a fraction of a degree each, straightening on
  hover. It did not earn its place: with six cards on an even grid, all the
  same width, the tilt read as a rendering fault rather than as a deliberate
  scatter. Removed rather than tuned – it would want cards of differing sizes
  to work at all.
#}
{#
  rise-stagger-2 + rise: cards rise in as they enter the viewport, the
  right-hand card of each row trailing its neighbour (see tailwind.css).
#}
{#
  mb-20 separates the strip from the gallery block below it. Spacing runs
  downwards, so the gap belongs to the section above rather than to the
  gallery – and it is harmless on a page where the strip stands alone.
#}
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-stretch gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 rise-stagger-2 mb-20">
  {% for row in rows %}
    <div{{ row.attributes.addClass('flex', 'rise') }}>
      {{- row.content -}}
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
